  "result": "I withdrew the LVMC_11_60_040 record as an `atom` gap on span `s1` and wrote the withdrawal to `record.jsonl`; I didn't revise the record.\n\n**Why no revision can pass:** the run's reading lists no included class for the aggregate `DEF-LVMC-11-02-140::taxicab`, and it marks `ru.taxicab` as unresolved. So the subject class (on `s1`, and the same aggregate on `s5`) can never be true: it is unknown for any taxicab and false for everything else. That is why forbid, permit, blind and branch_1 all came back unknown with `aggregate_unresolved`. Changing the record's mapping can't fix this. Swapping in `ru.taxicab` directly isn't an option, because the `ru.aggregate` contract says an admitted aggregate stays an aggregate.\n\n**What the operator needs to decide (either one unblocks it):**\n- **Treat the markings as the licence:** read \"properly licensed under State and local law\" through the taxicab's markings (an `observable_reading` of category `status`). `ru.taxicab` is then classified as included in the aggregate.\n- **Add a class atom:** create one whose contract carries the licence to provide taxicab service.\n\nOnce either is decided, the coder's existing rule and witnesses should need no change.",
